1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--levels-of-comprehension","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/levels-of-comprehension","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/levels-of-comprehension","sourceHash":"ea6ba044e5c1367e698c0a27d18b8b8e78d85e9816ce62660ae7066162b5c24c","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:19.006Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Levels of Comprehension","zh":"理解能力等级"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When talking about language learning, it's very useful to have a \"standardized\" system for evaluating comprehension. The goal of this article is to give you a clear and useful framework for thinking about your progress and understanding of your target language.","zh":"谈论语言学习时，有一套用于评估理解能力的“标准化”体系会非常实用。本文旨在为你提供一个清晰实用的框架，帮助你思考自己的学习进度以及对目标语言的理解程度。"}},{"id":"about-the-model","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"About the Model","zh":"关于这个模型"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"In the original Refold Roadmap, we used a much simpler system with just six levels ranging from total beginner to absolute mastery. This system was too simple and the gaps between the levels was very inconsistent.","zh":"在最初的 Refold 路线图中，我们使用的是一套简单得多的体系，只有六个等级，范围从完全的初学者到彻底掌握。这套体系过于简单，各等级之间的跨度也很不一致。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But more importantly, it left out some very crucial nuance.","zh":"但更重要的是，它忽略了一些至关重要的细微差别。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Comprehension is just a single part of a larger question. If you understand a TV show made for kids quite easily, that doesn't mean you'll understand a movie for adults, despite it being \"in the same language.\"","zh":"理解能力只是一个更大问题中的一个方面。如果你能轻松理解一部面向儿童制作的电视节目，并不意味着你也能理解成人电影，即使二者使用的是“同一种语言”。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The six level system also left out the important factor of \"how difficult is it to understand.\" Using 100% of your energy and focus to understand is very different from being able to achieve the same level of understanding while also washing dishes and cooking dinner.","zh":"六级体系还忽略了“理解起来有多难”这一重要因素。必须投入全部精力和注意力才能理解，与一边洗碗做饭、一边达到同样的理解程度，是截然不同的情况。"}},{"id":"rate-of-perceived-exertion","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Rate of Perceived Exertion","zh":"主观用力程度"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"An issue with many method of measuring comprehension is that people are generally bad at estimating percentages (what does 70% comprehension mean? 70% of the words? 70% of the sentences? 70% of the meaning? Are you positive it's actually 70% and that's not just a rough estimate?).","zh":"许多理解能力衡量方法都有一个问题：人们通常不擅长估算百分比（理解 70% 到底是什么意思？理解了 70% 的单词、70% 的句子，还是 70% 的含义？你确定真的有 70%，而不只是一个粗略估计吗？）。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This problem is hard to solve, but a system that works rather well is known as \"rate of perceived exertion\" and is often used in personal fitness and at the gym. Basically, you give a number between 1-10 based on how much you feel like you're pushing your body.","zh":"这个问题很难解决，但有一套效果相当不错的体系，称为“主观用力程度”，经常用于个人健身和健身房训练。简单来说，你根据自己感觉身体有多用力，给出一个 1 到 10 之间的数字。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"1 means it's taking no more effort that sitting and breathing. And 10 means you cannot possibly do any more. 7 is a difficult pace, but you could keep it up, despite heavy breathing.","zh":"1 表示所需的力气不比坐着呼吸更多；10 则表示你已经完全无法再继续。7 代表颇具挑战的强度：虽然会大口喘气，但仍可以维持下去。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This works because it's an internal guesstimate based on your current fitness level. And it's more useful because of that.","zh":"这套方法之所以有效，是因为它是依据你当前体能水平做出的个人主观估计。也正因如此，它更具实用性。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It's also very useful for language learning. Although it's not exactly about exertion. Maybe Rate of Perceived Comprehension is better.","zh":"它对语言学习也非常实用，尽管这里衡量的并不完全是用力程度。也许称为“主观理解程度”更合适。"}},{"id":"putting-them-together","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Putting them Together","zh":"将两者结合起来"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"To figure out your level of comprehension, we're actually going to combine a few different numbers: your rate of perceived comprehension and rate of perceived effort.","zh":"为了确定你的理解能力等级，我们实际上要将几个不同的数字结合起来：你的主观理解程度和主观用力程度。"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"These charts are meant to give you a general idea of what each level is, but your own <em>feeling</em> of understanding and effort is what matters. The differences between level 5 and 6 is pretty small and is impossible to objectively measure.","zh":"这些表格旨在让你大致了解每个等级，但真正重要的是你自己对理解程度和所需精力的<em>感受</em>。第 5 级和第 6 级之间的差别很小，无法进行客观衡量。"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Level","zh":"等级","header":true},{"en":"Comprehension Amount","zh":"理解程度","header":true}],[{"en":"1","zh":"1","header":false},{"en":"You can hardly tell what language it is, let alone understand words","zh":"你几乎连这是什么语言都判断不出来，更不用说理解单词了","header":false}],[{"en":"2","zh":"2","header":false},{"en":"You can make out a few common words, but not much more than that","zh":"你能辨认出几个常用词，但也仅此而已","header":false}],[{"en":"3","zh":"3","header":false},{"en":"You can't understand much overall, but frequently recognize and understand individual words or phrases","zh":"整体上理解不了多少，但经常能认出并理解个别单词或短语","header":false}],[{"en":"4","zh":"4","header":false},{"en":"You know and understand the majority of words, and can often guess at the topic, but you're not sure how correct that guess is","zh":"你认识并理解大多数单词，也经常能猜出主题，但不确定自己的猜测有多准确","header":false}],[{"en":"5","zh":"5","header":false},{"en":"You can tell what's being discussed and generally what people think","zh":"你能判断大家在讨论什么，也大致知道他们的看法","header":false}],[{"en":"6","zh":"6","header":false},{"en":"You can follow along, but frequently lose the thread of what's happening","zh":"你能跟上内容，但经常会跟丢情节或思路","header":false}],[{"en":"7","zh":"7","header":false},{"en":"You understand the plot and most of the language, but often notice words that you don't know","zh":"你能理解情节和大部分语言内容，但经常会注意到自己不认识的单词","header":false}],[{"en":"8","zh":"8","header":false},{"en":"You're able to understand and enjoy the content, but miss a few things, but not enough to limit your understanding","zh":"你能够理解并享受内容，虽然会漏掉少量信息，但并不足以妨碍整体理解","header":false}],[{"en":"9","zh":"9","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Level","zh":"等级","header":true},{"en":"Effort Required","zh":"所需精力","header":true}],[{"en":"1","zh":"1","header":false},{"en":"You could put together a puzzle or Lego while easily maintaining this level of comprehension","zh":"你可以一边拼拼图或搭乐高，一边轻松保持这一理解程度","header":false}],[{"en":"2","zh":"2","header":false},{"en":"You could do fairly complex, but repetitive tasks that don't require much thought","zh":"你可以同时完成相当复杂但具有重复性、不太需要思考的任务","header":false}],[{"en":"3","zh":"3","header":false},{"en":"You could do light activities (such as housework or exercise)","zh":"你可以同时进行轻度活动（例如做家务或锻炼）","header":false}],[{"en":"4","zh":"4","header":false},{"en":"You can only do very light activities that don't have major distraction potential (walking or painting a wall, but probably not cleaning the bathroom)","zh":"你只能同时做不太容易分散注意力的轻微活动（例如散步或粉刷墙壁，但大概不能打扫卫生间）","header":false}],[{"en":"5","zh":"5","header":false},{"en":"You're using a normal amount of effort and not getting too distracted, about the level of effort you'd need to watch a TV show in your native language","zh":"你投入的精力适中，也不会过于分心，大致相当于用母语观看电视节目时所需的精力","header":false}],[{"en":"6","zh":"6","header":false},{"en":"You need to choose to be focused on what you're doing, but don't feel much particular effort","zh":"你需要有意识地专注于当前内容，但不会感觉特别费力","header":false}],[{"en":"7","zh":"7","header":false},{"en":"You need to put in some moderate effort to maintain this level of comprehension, but still don't feel particularly high effort","zh":"你需要投入适度的精力才能保持这一理解程度，但仍不会觉得特别吃力","header":false}],[{"en":"8","zh":"8","header":false},{"en":"You're locked in and focused, but it's starting to become difficult to maintain that focus for longer periods of time (30+ minutes)","zh":"你已经全神贯注，但长时间（30 分钟以上）维持这种专注开始变得困难","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When you find your level of comprehension and effort, put them together for your level of comprehension!","zh":"确定自己的理解程度和用力程度后，将两者结合起来，作为你的理解能力等级！"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"And ideally, if you're mentioning it to someone or recording it, include the type of content you're judging against. That way, the level is tied to content level, making it more useful.","zh":"如果你要向别人描述或记录这个等级，最好同时注明作为评估依据的内容类型。这样，等级就能与内容难度关联起来，也会更有参考价值。"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Here's a list of (some) content types <em>roughly</em> in order of difficulty.","zh":"下面列出（部分）内容类型，并按难度<em>大致</em>排序。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Content Type","zh":"内容类型","header":true},{"en":"Example","zh":"示例","header":true}],[{"en":"Super Beginner Comprehensible Input","zh":"零基础可理解输入","header":false},{"en":"Dreaming Spanish Super Beginner","zh":"Dreaming Spanish 零基础内容","header":false}],[{"en":"Toddler Content","zh":"幼儿内容","header":false},{"en":"Peppa Pig","zh":"《小猪佩奇》","header":false}],[{"en":"Beginner Comprehensible Input","zh":"初级可理解输入","header":false},{"en":"Dreaming Spanish Beginner","zh":"Dreaming Spanish 初级内容","header":false}],[{"en":"Children's Content/For the Family","zh":"儿童或合家欢内容","header":false},{"en":"Disney Movies","zh":"迪士尼电影","header":false}],[{"en":"Intermediate Comprehensible Input","zh":"中级可理解输入","header":false},{"en":"Dreaming Spanish Intermediate","zh":"Dreaming Spanish 中级内容","header":false}],[{"en":"\"My First Chapter Book\"","zh":"“我的第一本章节书”","header":false},{"en":"The Magic Treehouse","zh":"《神奇树屋》","header":false}],[{"en":"Graded Reader","zh":"分级读物","header":false},{"en":"Short Stories in {language}","zh":"《{language}短篇故事》","header":false}],[{"en":"Simple Dramas or TV shows","zh":"情节简单的电视剧或电视节目","header":false},{"en":"Slice of Life anime","zh":"日常系动画","header":false}],[{"en":"Advanced Comprehensible Input","zh":"高级可理解输入","header":false},{"en":"Dreaming Spanish Advanced","zh":"Dreaming Spanish 高级内容","header":false}],[{"en":"Travel or Daily Vlogs","zh":"旅行或日常 Vlog","header":false},{"en":"Casey Neistat","zh":"Casey Neistat","header":false}],[{"en":"Generic YouTube","zh":"普通 YouTube 视频","header":false},{"en":"<template></template>","zh":"<template></template>","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are many more content types than just these and the lines between them might be blurred. But this chart should help you find where, more or less, the piece of content you're using would fall in terms of difficulty.","zh":"实际的内容类型远不止这些，它们之间的界限也可能比较模糊。不过，这张表应该能帮助你大致判断自己所用内容在难度上处于什么位置。"}},{"id":"how-it-might-look","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How it might look","zh":"实际情况可能是什么样"}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Now that you know the general idea and levels, let's look at a few examples of various levels of comprehension and effort. These are examples from my own language learning (at time of writing):","zh":"现在你已经了解了基本思路和各个等级，接下来看看理解程度与用力程度的几个不同示例。这些例子来自我本人在撰写本文时的语言学习情况："}},{"id":"mandarin","type":"heading","level":4,"content":{"en":"Mandarin","zh":"普通话"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>I can understand the simple drama I'm watching at about a 6 or 7 level of comprehension, but it takes at least level 8 effort.</p>","zh":"<p>我观看情节简单的电视剧时，理解程度大约为 6 级或 7 级，但至少需要投入 8 级的精力。</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>And when I watch intermediate podcasts (made for learners), I understand at a solid 8, as long as I'm putting in level 7 effort or more.</p>","zh":"<p>观看为学习者制作的中级播客时，只要投入 7 级或更高的精力，我就能稳定达到 8 级的理解程度。</p>"}},{"id":"czech","type":"heading","level":4,"content":{"en":"Czech","zh":"捷克语"}},{"id":"segment-0031","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>I can read plays at an 8 or 9 level of understanding with a level 6 level of focus and the help of a dictionary. But it's easy to do.</p>","zh":"<p>借助词典并投入 6 级的专注度，我阅读剧本时可以达到 8 级或 9 级的理解程度，而且读起来很轻松。</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0033","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>I watch simpler YouTube without too much trouble, maybe level 5-6 focus and a fairly comfortable 9 level of understanding. But if I put on something more complicated, like a news recap, I need to focus more, around level 7-8, and usually only understand at level 7 unless I can look up all the specialized vocab.</p>","zh":"<p>观看比较简单的 YouTube 视频时，我不会觉得太困难，大概只需 5–6 级的专注度，就能相当轻松地达到 9 级理解程度。但如果换成更复杂的内容，例如新闻回顾，我就需要更加专注，大约达到 7–8 级，而且除非能查清所有专业词汇，否则通常只能达到 7 级理解程度。</p>"}},{"id":"spanish","type":"heading","level":4,"content":{"en":"Spanish","zh":"西班牙语"}},{"id":"segment-0036","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>I can listen to an audiobook at level 9 understanding with level 2 effort.</p>","zh":"<p>我只需投入 2 级的精力，就能以 9 级的理解程度收听有声书。</p>"}},{"id":"segment-0038","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p>But when I get together with friends, understanding drops to more like a 7 or 8, but I'm not really trying that hard, usually only a 6 level of effort.</p>","zh":"<p>但和朋友聚会时，我的理解程度会降到 7 级或 8 级左右。不过我并没有特别努力去听，通常只投入 6 级的精力。</p>"}},{"id":"practical-example-harry-potter","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Practical Example: Harry Potter","zh":"实际示例：《哈利·波特》"}},{"id":"segment-0041","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Here is the first paragraph of Harry Potter and the Sorcerer’s Stone:","zh":"以下是《哈利·波特与魔法石》的第一段："}},{"id":"segment-0042","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say that they were perfectly normal, thank you very much. They were the last people you’d expect to be involved in anything strange or mysterious, because they just didn’t hold with such nonsense.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>住在女贞路四号的德思礼夫妇总是得意地说，他们是再正常不过的人了，多谢关心。他们绝不会和任何稀奇古怪、神神秘秘的事扯上关系，因为他们根本无法容忍那种无稽之谈。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0044","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The original Roadmap had some \"examples\" of different levels of understanding, using the first paragraph of Harry Potter to demonstrate what each level would feel like if you were an English learner trying to read Harry Potter.","zh":"最初的路线图使用《哈利·波特》的第一段，给出了不同理解等级的一些“示例”，展示英语学习者尝试阅读《哈利·波特》时，各个等级大致会是什么感受。"}},{"id":"segment-0045","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Unknown words have been replaced with gibberish. Other words and phrases have been swapped out with similar English words to represent when the learner knows the word but isn’t able to grasp its usage in the specific context. We’ve marked these with a “*”.","zh":"其中不认识的单词被替换成了胡言乱语。其他单词和短语则被替换为意思相近的英语表达，用来表示学习者虽然认识这个单词，却无法理解它在特定语境中的用法。我们用“*”标出了这些地方。"}},{"id":"level-2-something","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 2: Something","zh":"第 2 级：好像在说些什么"}},{"id":"segment-0047","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Pe and Per Dursley, of camer embe, Privet Unfax, were preth to say that quiga were counges kepter, *gratitude very slamy. Quiga were the pilso olical themic novatial to be vitimese in theoloney unittlem or writuence, because quiga atter inson voler rotes evere disgushese.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>Pe 和 Per Dursley，住在 camer embe、Privet Unfax，preth 地说 quiga 是 counges kepter，*感谢，非常 slamy。Quiga 是你最不会 olical themic novatial 会 vitimese 于 theoloney unittlem 或 writuence 的 pilso 人，因为 quiga atter inson voler rotes evere disgushese。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0049","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You recognize some individual words such as “and”, “to”, “were”, and “thank you”, but you don’t have the slightest idea what the paragraph is about.","zh":"你能认出“and”“to”“were”和“thank you”等个别词语，但完全不知道这一段在讲什么。"}},{"id":"level-4-bits-and-pieces","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 4: Bits and Pieces","zh":"第 4 级：零碎片段"}},{"id":"segment-0051","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Pe and Per Dursley, of camer four, Privet Unfax, were preth to say that they were counges kepter, *gratitude very slamy. They were the pilso people themic novatial to be vitimese in theoloney unittlem or writuence, because they just didn’t voler with such disgushese.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>Pe 和 Per Dursley，住在 camer four、Privet Unfax，preth 地说他们是 counges kepter，*感谢，非常 slamy。他们是你最不会 themic novatial 会 vitimese 于 theoloney unittlem 或 writuence 的 pilso 人，因为他们就是不愿 voler 这种 disgushese。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0053","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You understand around half of the individual words. This allows you to glean that the paragraph seems to be talking about a group of people.","zh":"你能理解大约一半的单词，因此可以看出这一段似乎在谈论一群人。"}},{"id":"level-5-gist","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 5: Gist","zh":"第 5 级：大意"}},{"id":"segment-0055","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of letter four, Privet Move, were preth to say that they were counges normal, *I show you gratitude. They were the *final people you’d expect to be vitimese in anything strange or writuence, because they just didn’t *carry with such disgushese.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>Dursley 先生和夫人，住在 Privet Move 四号，preth 地说他们是 counges 正常的人，*我向你表示感谢。他们是你最不会想到会 vitimese 于任何奇怪或 writuence 事情的*最后的人，因为他们就是不愿*携带这种 disgushese。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0057","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You understand that the paragraph is talking about two people named “Mr. and Mrs. Dursley”. You’re pretty sure the point of the paragraph is to describe them as “normal”.","zh":"你明白这一段谈论的是两个名叫“Dursley 先生和夫人”的人。你相当确定，这一段的重点是把他们描述为“正常人”。"}},{"id":"segment-0058","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You know most of the words, but there are several you’ve never seen before. You don’t understand what “number four, Privet Drive” is because you think that “drive” means “to move a car”. You know what “thank you very much” means but you’ve interpreted it as “I show you gratitude”, so you’re confused as to why it’s being used in this context. You know the word “last” means “final”, but you can’t make sense of this particular usage. Same with “hold” and “carry”. Nevertheless, you’re able to infer from context that the sentence is likely saying that the Dursleys are not strange.","zh":"你认识大多数单词，但仍有几个从未见过。你不明白“number four, Privet Drive”是什么意思，因为你以为“drive”只表示“开车”。你知道“thank you very much”的意思，却把它理解成了“我向你表示感谢”，所以不明白它为什么会出现在这个语境中。你知道“last”可以表示“最后的”，但无法理解它在这里的具体用法。“hold”和“carry”也是如此。尽管如此，你仍能根据上下文推断，这句话可能是在说 Dursley 一家并不奇怪。"}},{"id":"level-6-story","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 6: Story","zh":"第 6 级：故事脉络"}},{"id":"segment-0060","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say that they were perfectly normal, *I show you gratitude. They were the last people you’d expect to be involved in anything strange or writuence, because they just didn’t *carry with such nonsense.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>住在 Privet Drive 四号的 Dursley 先生和夫人自豪地说，他们是再正常不过的人了，*我向你表示感谢。他们绝不会和任何奇怪或 writuence 的事情扯上关系，因为他们就是不愿*携带这种无稽之谈。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0062","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There is only one word you don’t know. You understand that the paragraph is talking about two people named “Mr. and Mrs. Dursley”, who feel strongly about being “normal”, and perhaps even have a dislike for people who are “not normal”.","zh":"你只有一个单词不认识。你明白这一段谈论的是两个名叫“Dursley 先生和夫人”的人。他们非常在意自己是否“正常”，甚至可能不喜欢那些“不正常”的人。"}},{"id":"segment-0063","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You’re still confused about what “thank you very much” is doing at the end of the first sentence. You aren’t familiar with the particular usage of “hold” in the second sentence, but you can infer from context that it probably means something along the lines of, “they don’t put up with such nonsense”.","zh":"你仍然不明白“thank you very much”为什么会出现在第一句话末尾。你不熟悉第二句话中“hold”的这种特定用法，但可以根据上下文推断，它的意思大概类似于“他们无法容忍这种无稽之谈”。"}},{"id":"level-8-comfortable","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 8: Comfortable","zh":"第 8 级：轻松理解"}},{"id":"segment-0065","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say that they were perfectly normal, thank you very much. They were the last people you’d expect to be involved in anything strange or mysterious, because they just didn’t hold with such nonsense.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>住在女贞路四号的德思礼夫妇总是得意地说，他们是再正常不过的人了，多谢关心。他们绝不会和任何稀奇古怪、神神秘秘的事扯上关系，因为他们根本无法容忍那种无稽之谈。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0067","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are no unknown words and you understand exactly what the core meaning of the paragraph is.","zh":"没有任何不认识的单词，而且你完全理解这一段的核心含义。"}},{"id":"segment-0068","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By this point, you are only missing out on nuance. You have a general sense of what “thank you very much” means in this context, but you don’t fully grasp that the tone conveys that the Dursleys are proud and obstinate people. You understand that “you’d” means “you would”, but you’re unable to perceive how this use of a contraction subtly changes the feel of the sentence. You also don’t pick up on the subtle way that “just” adds emphasis in the last sentence.","zh":"到这个阶段，你欠缺的只是对细微含义的把握。你大致知道“非常感谢”在这个语境中是什么意思，但还没有完全领会这种语气所传达的意思：德思礼夫妇既自负又固执。你明白“you’d”是“you would”的缩写，却感受不到使用这种缩写会如何微妙地改变句子的感觉。你也没有察觉到最后一句中的“just”以一种细微的方式加强了语气。"}},{"id":"segment-0069","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You need to think about these subtleties and nuances, but native speakers perceive them automatically and instinctively.","zh":"你需要思考才能体会这些细节和微妙之处，而母语者会自然而本能地感受到它们。"}},{"id":"level-9-near-automatic","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Level 9: Near Automatic","zh":"第 9 级：接近自动理解"}},{"id":"segment-0071","type":"blockquote","content":{"en":"<p><em>Mr. and Mrs. Dursley, of number four, Privet Drive, were proud to say that they were ganbly normal, thank you very much. They were the last people you’d expect to be involved in anything strange or mysterious, because they just didn’t hold with such nonsense.</em></p>","zh":"<p><em>住在女贞路四号的德思礼先生和夫人非常自豪地宣称，他们是再正常不过的人了，多谢。他们最不可能卷入任何古怪或神秘的事情，因为他们压根儿不接受这种无稽之谈。</em></p>"}},{"id":"segment-0073","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You effortlessly understand the paragraph, despite not knowing a word, but you're about to easily tell that it's not important to the overall story and that it's an intensifier. You are effectively understanding at a native level.","zh":"尽管有一个词不认识，你仍然能毫不费力地理解这段话，而且马上就能轻松判断出，这个词对整体故事并不重要，只是一个加强语气的词。实际上，你已经达到了母语者水平的理解能力。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
